359
00:31:11,039 --> 00:31:14,559
-Linda, wait a minute. Hold it, hold--
-I'm going to leave. We are leaving.

360
00:31:19,719 --> 00:31:23,679
It was right then that I started
thinking about Thomas Jefferson...

361
00:31:24,999 --> 00:31:27,479
...the Declaration of Independence...

362
00:31:27,799 --> 00:31:33,759
...and the part about our right to life,
liberty and the pursuit of happiness.

363
00:31:33,999 --> 00:31:35,799
And I remember thinking:

364
00:31:35,999 --> 00:31:40,399
How did he know
to put the "pursuit" part in there?

365
00:31:40,599 --> 00:31:45,279
That maybe happiness is something
that we can only pursue.

366
00:31:45,479 --> 00:31:48,519
And maybe we can actually
never have it...

367
00:31:48,879 --> 00:31:50,519
...no matter what.

368
00:31:50,719 --> 00:31:52,439
How did he know that?

369
00:31:57,679 --> 00:32:00,479
Linda. Linda.

370
00:32:33,399 --> 00:32:35,119
-Hello?
-Chris.

371
00:32:35,319 --> 00:32:37,919
-Who is this?
-Jay Twistle.

372
00:32:38,799 --> 00:32:40,599
-Hey.
-Dean Witter.

373
00:32:40,799 --> 00:32:43,519
Yeah, of course. How are you?

374
00:32:43,719 --> 00:32:46,199
I'm fine. Listen, do you still
wanna come in and talk?

375
00:32:46,399 --> 00:32:47,639
Yes, sir. Absolutely.

376
00:32:47,839 --> 00:32:50,759
I'll tell you what. Come on by
day after tomorrow, in the morning.

377
00:32:50,959 --> 00:32:54,719
We're interviewing for the internships.
You got a pen and paper?

378
00:32:54,959 --> 00:32:56,479
Yes. Yes, I do.

379
00:32:59,479 --> 00:33:02,239
-Hold on one second.
-All right.

380
00:33:06,119 --> 00:33:08,239
Hello?

381
00:33:08,439 --> 00:33:10,759
-Chris?
-Go ahead. I have one.

382
00:33:10,999 --> 00:33:13,599
Write this number down so you can
call my secretary, Janice.

383
00:33:13,799 --> 00:33:15,879
-She can give you all the specifics.
-Yep.

384
00:33:16,079 --> 00:33:17,959
-Okay, 41 5.
-41 5.

385
00:33:18,159 --> 00:33:19,839
-864.
-864.

386
00:33:20,039 --> 00:33:22,079
-0256.
-0256.

387
00:33:22,279 --> 00:33:25,279
-Yeah, extension 4796.
-4796.

388
00:33:25,479 --> 00:33:29,759
-Right. Call her tomorrow.
-Yes, sir. 41 5-864-0256.

389
00:33:29,959 --> 00:33:31,279
-Okay, buddy.
-All right, yes.

390
00:33:31,479 --> 00:33:33,639
-Thank you very much.
-We'll see you soon.

391
00:33:34,399 --> 00:33:37,559
864-0256.

392
00:33:37,759 --> 00:33:40,959
4796. Janice.

393
00:33:43,999 --> 00:33:45,839
-Chris.
-Hey.

394
00:33:46,039 --> 00:33:48,319
Did you--? Have you seen
Linda and Christopher?

395
00:33:48,519 --> 00:33:50,399
-No. You catch the game last night?
-No, no.

396
00:33:50,599 --> 00:33:51,999
You didn't see that, 1 1 8, 1 --?

397
00:33:52,199 --> 00:33:54,399
Excuse me, did Linda
and Christopher come in here?

398
00:33:54,599 --> 00:33:58,239
-No, I haven't see them.
-1 1 9-1 20. Double overtime.

399
00:33:58,479 --> 00:34:00,599
Moons hits a three-pointer
at 1 7 seconds left.

400
00:34:00,799 --> 00:34:02,399
Wayne, Wayne, Wayne.

401
00:34:02,599 --> 00:34:04,719
Can't talk to you
about numbers right now.

402
00:34:04,919 --> 00:34:07,559
-What's your problem with numbers?
-864-2....

403
00:34:07,759 --> 00:34:09,719
-And you owe me money.
-Yeah.

404
00:34:09,919 --> 00:34:11,679
You owe me $1 4.

405
00:34:11,879 --> 00:34:13,719
I'm gonna get that to you.

406
00:34:14,599 --> 00:34:17,079
I need my money.
I need my money.

407
00:34:18,199 --> 00:34:20,279
Fourteen's a number.

408
00:34:46,719 --> 00:34:49,959
Hey, don't you ever take my son
away from me again.

409
00:34:50,159 --> 00:34:51,439
-You hear me?
-Leave me alone!

410
00:34:51,639 --> 00:34:53,479
Don't take my son away
from me again.

411
00:34:53,679 --> 00:34:55,439
Do you understand
what I'm saying to you?

412
00:34:55,639 --> 00:34:58,959
Don't you walk away from me when
I'm talking to you. Do you hear me?

413
00:34:59,159 --> 00:35:00,679
-Do you wanna leave?
-Yeah.

414
00:35:00,879 --> 00:35:03,719
-You wanna leave?
-Yes, I want to leave!

415
00:35:04,959 --> 00:35:06,839
Get the hell out of here,
then, Linda.

416
00:35:07,039 --> 00:35:09,559
Get the hell out of here.
Christopher's staying with me.

417
00:35:09,759 --> 00:35:12,079
You're the one that dragged
us down. You hear me?

418
00:35:12,279 --> 00:35:15,359
-You are so weak.
-No. I am not happy anymore.

419
00:35:15,559 --> 00:35:18,159
-I'm just not happy!
-Then go get happy, Linda!

420
00:35:18,359 --> 00:35:19,719
Just go get happy.

421
00:35:20,279 --> 00:35:22,159
But Christopher's living with me.

422
00:35:22,359 --> 00:35:24,159
-Stop!
-Did you hear what I said?

423
00:35:24,439 --> 00:35:26,839
Christopher's living with me!

424
00:35:52,999 --> 00:35:55,959
Hey. Come on, let's go.

425
00:35:56,159 --> 00:35:58,479
-How you doing, Mrs. Chu?
-Hi.

426
00:36:02,159 --> 00:36:04,719
-Where's Mom?
-Look, just get your stuff.

427
00:36:04,919 --> 00:36:08,359
But she told me she was
coming to pick me up today.

428
00:36:08,599 --> 00:36:10,599
Yeah, I know.

429
00:36:11,759 --> 00:36:16,399
I talked to Mom earlier.
Everything's fine, okay?

430
00:36:21,839 --> 00:36:24,039
Where do I sleep tonight?

431
00:36:24,239 --> 00:36:26,359
Let me ask you something.
Are you happy?

432
00:36:26,559 --> 00:36:29,239
-Yeah.
-All right. Because I'm happy.

433
00:36:29,439 --> 00:36:32,919
And if you're happy and I'm happy,
then that's a good thing, right?

434
00:36:33,119 --> 00:36:34,639
-Yeah.
-All right.

435
00:36:34,839 --> 00:36:36,879
You're sleeping with me.

436
00:36:37,079 --> 00:36:41,759
You're staying at home,
where you belong, all right?

437
00:36:56,199 --> 00:36:57,879
Christopher.

438
00:37:15,439 --> 00:37:18,239
Hey, listen. I need the rent.

439
00:37:18,479 --> 00:37:19,879
I can't wait anymore.

440
00:37:20,079 --> 00:37:22,479
Yeah, I'm good for that, Charlie.
I'm gonna get it.

441
00:37:22,679 --> 00:37:25,719
Why don't you go two blocks over
at the Mission lnn motel?

442
00:37:25,919 --> 00:37:27,479
It's half what you pay here.

443
00:37:27,719 --> 00:37:31,119
Listen, Chris. I need you out
