01:16:34,399 --> 01:16:36,759
-Dressed yet?
-No.

955
01:16:40,599 --> 01:16:43,959
Chris! Chris!
Don't jerk me around, okay, Chris?

956
01:16:44,159 --> 01:16:46,919
I'm not jerking you around, Ralph,
all right? I'm gonna get it.

957
01:16:47,119 --> 01:16:50,679
-I need that money now, not later.
-When I get it, you get it, Ralph.

958
01:16:50,879 --> 01:16:52,799
Now!

959
01:16:56,439 --> 01:16:58,519
Hey, what's happening, man?

960
01:16:58,759 --> 01:17:01,639
Wayne, I need to get
that $1 4 from you.

961
01:17:03,319 --> 01:17:05,159
I thought I didn't owe you that now.

962
01:17:05,359 --> 01:17:08,439
-What? Why?
-Why what?

963
01:17:08,639 --> 01:17:10,999
Why would you think
you don't owe me my money?

964
01:17:11,199 --> 01:17:13,199
I helped you move.

965
01:17:15,399 --> 01:17:18,319
You drove me two blocks, Wayne.

966
01:17:18,519 --> 01:17:20,279
That's 200 yards.

967
01:17:20,479 --> 01:17:22,439
It's been four months, Wayne.

968
01:17:22,639 --> 01:17:26,239
I need my money. I need my money.
I need my money right now.

969
01:17:26,439 --> 01:17:28,759
-I don't have it, man. I'm sorry.
-Go get my money.

970
01:17:28,959 --> 01:17:31,199
-Wayne, get my mo--
-I really don't, man. It's $1 4.

971
01:17:31,399 --> 01:17:33,079
It's my $1 4!
Go get my money!

972
01:17:33,319 --> 01:17:35,879
-All of this for $1 4.
-Get my money, Wayne.

973
01:17:54,239 --> 01:17:56,399
Dad, look at me!

974
01:17:56,839 --> 01:17:58,559
Dad.

975
01:17:59,559 --> 01:18:03,079
-Should I go?
-Sure, man. Why not?

976
01:18:19,159 --> 01:18:20,199
-Stay here.
-Dad, look.

977
01:18:20,399 --> 01:18:21,999
-No, no. Stay right here.
-Dad.

978
01:18:22,199 --> 01:18:24,999
Did you hear what I said?
Did you hear me?

979
01:18:30,079 --> 01:18:33,599
-Dad, where you going?
-Hey, what did I say?

980
01:18:36,639 --> 01:18:38,239
Dad!

981
01:18:38,479 --> 01:18:41,879
Dad, wait! Dad!

982
01:18:49,999 --> 01:18:52,079
-Dad.
-I gotta--

983
01:18:52,279 --> 01:18:55,639
I gotta get back to the '60s, man.
That's what I wanna do.

984
01:18:55,839 --> 01:19:00,159
When I was younger. I wanna see
Jimi Hendrix do that guitar on fire.

985
01:19:03,239 --> 01:19:05,919
Bring back my time machine!

986
01:19:07,279 --> 01:19:08,919
Bring my time machine back!

987
01:19:17,799 --> 01:19:21,399
-Dad, where are we going?
-Just be quiet.

988
01:19:21,999 --> 01:19:24,759
Go get your things. Go.

989
01:19:47,919 --> 01:19:49,639
-Chris?
-Yes.

990
01:19:49,839 --> 01:19:53,759
Dr. Telm can't get back to meet you.
I'm sorry.

991
01:20:04,919 --> 01:20:07,399
Where are we going now?

992
01:20:08,159 --> 01:20:11,439
Gotta-- We gotta
see somebody else.

993
01:20:13,519 --> 01:20:15,639
I'm tired.

994
01:20:17,679 --> 01:20:19,279
I know.

995
01:20:26,679 --> 01:20:30,759
Doesn't seem to be functioning
right now.

996
01:20:31,199 --> 01:20:33,519
-I have to go now, Chris.
-No, no, no.

997
01:20:33,719 --> 01:20:37,599
Just give me a second. I'm sure
I'm gonna be able to figure it out.

998
01:20:39,399 --> 01:20:41,679
Chris. Chris, just come back
when it's working.

999
01:20:41,879 --> 01:20:44,719
-No, no. I have to fix it now.
-No.

1000
01:20:44,919 --> 01:20:50,159
Look, I'll still be putting money
in the office, then, all right?

1001
01:20:50,359 --> 01:20:52,479
I really have to go, Chris.

1002
01:20:53,719 --> 01:20:55,399
Thank you. Thank you.

1003
01:20:55,599 --> 01:20:57,479
Thank you for your time.
I appreciate it.

1004
01:20:57,679 --> 01:20:59,359
I'll see you soon.

1005
01:21:51,359 --> 01:21:53,799
Why are our things here?

1006
01:21:54,799 --> 01:21:56,439
Dad.

1007
01:22:38,959 --> 01:22:41,679
-Let's go. Come on.
-Where?

1008
01:22:43,279 --> 01:22:45,599
-Just out of here.
-Why?

1009
01:22:45,799 --> 01:22:48,799
-We can't stay here tonight.
-Yes, we can. Open the door!

1010
01:22:48,999 --> 01:22:51,999
-Did you hear what I said? Let's go.
-Open the door!

1011
01:22:53,679 --> 01:22:57,559
Hey, did you hear what I said?
Stop it.

1012
01:22:57,759 --> 01:22:59,239
Stop it.

1013
01:23:03,479 --> 01:23:04,959
Come on.

1014
01:23:14,039 --> 01:23:15,519
Come on.

1015
01:23:32,519 --> 01:23:34,199
Wayne!

1016
01:23:35,279 --> 01:23:37,159
Wayne!

1017
01:23:44,319 --> 01:23:46,679
Wayne!

1018
01:24:02,199 --> 01:24:05,919
Get up. Stand up. Come on.

1019
01:24:21,759 --> 01:24:23,799
Where are we going?

1020
01:24:25,999 --> 01:24:29,319
-Dad, where are we going?
-I don't know.

1021
01:24:44,799 --> 01:24:47,199
It's not a time machine.

1022
01:24:47,399 --> 01:24:48,839
Dad.

1023
01:24:49,199 --> 01:24:50,519
It's not a time machine.

1024
01:24:50,719 --> 01:24:53,999
The guy said it was a time machine.
It's not a time machine. He was wrong.

1025
01:24:54,399 --> 01:24:56,759
-What guy?
-The guy. He was at the park.

1026
01:24:56,999 --> 01:24:58,919
He said it was a time machine.

1027
01:25:05,239 --> 01:25:06,479
Yes, it is.

1028
01:25:08,039 --> 01:25:09,839
No, it's not.

1029
01:25:11,879 --> 01:25:13,839
-lt is.
-No, it's not.

1030
01:25:20,039 --> 01:25:24,559
All we gotta do is push
this black button right here.

1031
01:25:27,759 --> 01:25:28,919
Wanna push it?

1032
01:25:33,399 --> 01:25:35,079
Okay.

1033
01:25:36,639 --> 01:25:38,199
Come on.

1034
01:25:39,719 --> 01:25:41,359
Come on, man.

1035
01:25:47,039 --> 01:25:48,079
Right here.

1036
01:25:48,479 --> 01:25:50,079
Wait a minute.
Where you wanna go?

1037
01:25:50,439 --> 01:25:52,439
I don't know.
Some place from before.

1038
01:25:52,999 --> 01:25:54,239
You gotta close your eyes.

1039
01:25:54,519 --> 01:25:56,399
You close your eyes. I wanna see.

1040
01:25:58,559 --> 01:26:00,999
All right, come on.
We'll push it together.

1041
01:26:06,799 --> 01:26:08,599
You gotta close your eyes.
Close your eyes.

1042
01:26:09,319 --> 01:26:11,519
It takes a few seconds.

1043
01:26:13,919 --> 01:26:15,839
Oh, my goodness.

1044
01:26:16,039 --> 01:26:18,199
Open, open, open!

1045
01:26:21,599 --> 01:26:24,239
-What is it?
-Dinosaurs.

1046
01:26:24,479 --> 01:26:26,679
-Where?
-You don't see all these dinosaurs?

1047
01:26:28,039 --> 01:26:31,679
Look around.
Look at all these dinosaurs.

1048
01:26:33,439 --> 01:26:35,839
-Can you see them?
-Yeah.

1049
01:26:36,039 --> 01:26:37,439
Wait. Come on, come on.

1050
01:26:37,639 --> 01:26:38,959
-Wait, watch out.
-What is it?

1051
01:26:39,199 --> 01:26:41,239
Don't step in the fire.
We're cavemen.

1052
01:26:41,599 --> 01:26:43,839
We need this fire,
because there's no electricity...

1053
01:26:44,039 --> 01:26:45,439
...and it's cold out here, okay?

1054
01:26:46,159 --> 01:26:48,519
-Watch out!
-Whoa! Oh, my good-- A T. rex.

1055
01:26:48,719 --> 01:26:52,359
Get your stuff.
Get your stuff. Get it.

1056
01:26:53,319 --> 01:26:56,439
-We gotta find someplace safe.
-Like what?

1057
01:26:56,639 --> 01:26:58,599
We need a cave.

1058
01:26:58,799 --> 01:26:59,879
A cave?

1059
01:27:00,119 --> 01:27:02,119
-We gotta find a cave. Come on.
-Okay.

1060
01:27:02,319 --> 01:27:04,119
Come on, come on.

1061
01:27:05,679 --> 01:27:07,079
Watch your back! Look out.

1062
01:27:07,279 --> 01:27:09,319
Here it is. Here's a cave. Come on.

1063
01:27:09,519 --> 01:27:12,399
Right here, right here.
Go, go, go.

1064
01:27:12,599 --> 01:27:13,839
Go ahead. Get in.

1065
01:27:14,039 --> 01:27:15,919
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

1066
01:27:19,519 --> 01:27:23,279
-Are we safe?
-Yeah, I think so.

1067
01:28:31,239 --> 01:28:32,879
Hey.

1068
01:28:34,479 --> 01:28:36,119
-How you doing, Jay?
-I'm doing good.

1069
01:28:36,319 --> 01:28:37,759
How are you getting along?

1070
01:28:37,959 --> 01:28:40,159
-Good. I'm good.
-You doing good?

1071
01:28:40,359 --> 01:28:42,879
-How you doing?
-I'm doing great.

1072
01:28:44,039 --> 01:28:45,679
Where you going?

1073
01:28:48,959 --> 01:28:51,959
I-- Sacramento.

1074
01:28:52,639 --> 01:28:55,279
Because I'm trying to move
a couple guys from--

1075
01:28:55,479 --> 01:28:58,119
They're at PacBell,
and I'm trying to bring them over--

1076
01:28:58,319 --> 01:28:59,599
Get them over to us.

1077
01:28:59,799 --> 01:29:01,519
So they got me
going out there golfing.

1078
01:29:01,719 --> 01:29:03,559
Awesome.

1079
01:29:03,759 --> 01:29:05,719
Hey, let them win a round.

1080
01:29:10,879 --> 01:29:12,879
Deborah, someone's asking for you.

1081
01:29:13,119 --> 01:29:16,199
-Where?
-He's outside. Please come with me.

1082
01:29:24,039 --> 01:29:25,599
Hi.

1083
01:29:28,959 --> 01:29:31,479
-Can I ask you a question?
-Sure.

1084
01:29:33,719 --> 01:29:35,359
We need a room.

1085
01:29:35,959 --> 01:29:38,919
Just until I can fix this and sell it.

1086
01:29:39,119 --> 01:29:41,759
-There's just some glass work.
-Let me stop you right there.

1087
01:29:41,959 --> 01:29:44,439
-I wish I could help you--
-This is my son, Christopher.

1088
01:29:44,759 --> 01:29:46,759
-He's 5 years old.
-Hi, baby.

1089
01:29:46,959 --> 01:29:50,039
-We need some place to stay.
-Okay, and I would love to help you...

1090
01:29:50,239 --> 01:29:53,119
...but we don't take men here.
It's only women and children.

1091
01:29:53,319 --> 01:29:56,359
He can stay here, but you have
to find someplace else to go.

1092
01:29:56,559 --> 01:29:57,959
We gotta stay together.

1093
01:29:58,159 --> 01:29:59,559
We got-- We're--

1094
01:29:59,759 --> 01:30:01,559
-Okay, listen.
-You gotta have some place--

1095
01:30:01,799 --> 01:30:04,639
Try Glide Memorial.
The building books up at 5.

1096
01:30:04,839 --> 01:30:06,359
So you hurry up. There's a line.

1097
01:30:06,559 --> 01:30:09,959
-And where is it? Come on.
-Ellis and Jones.

1098
01:30:45,199 --> 01:30:50,839
Hey, everybody. We have
four spots left, and that's all.

1099
01:30:51,239 --> 01:30:54,119
-Man.
-Hey, come on, man.

1100
01:30:54,319 --> 01:30:55,519
-Come on.
-Come on, what?

1101
01:30:55,719 --> 01:30:57,319
-Hey, that's my spot.
-Back off.

1102
01:30:57,519 --> 01:30:59,959
Come on, don't do this to me.
Don't--

1103
01:31:02,359 --> 01:31:03,919
Dad!

1104
01:31:04,359 --> 01:31:06,399
Stop it! Break it up!
Break it up!

1105
01:31:06,599 --> 01:31:08,199
Stop! Stop!

1106
01:31:08,399 --> 01:31:10,719
Get out of the line, both of you.
Both of you.

1107
01:31:10,919 --> 01:31:13,519
I was here first. They told me
that we had to be on time.

1108
01:31:13,839 --> 01:31:15,759
I got here on time. I was in line.

1109
01:31:15,959 --> 01:31:17,719
I came from work, I got my son.

1110
01:31:17,919 --> 01:31:20,439
I was here on time.
We were here on time!

1111
01:31:20,679 --> 01:31:22,239
He sliced in front of him in line.

1112
01:31:22,479 --> 01:31:24,759
-Who did?
-He did.

1113
01:31:25,039 --> 01:31:29,559
Come on, come on, Rodney.
Come on. Let's go. Get out of line.

1114
01:31:38,799 --> 01:31:40,799
That's it. No more.

1115
01:31:47,839 --> 01:31:50,799
-What's your favorite color?
-Green.

1116
01:31:50,999 --> 01:31:52,239
Green?

1117
01:31:52,479 --> 01:31:55,439
-What do you like that's green?
-Trees.

1118
01:31:55,679 --> 01:31:58,639
Trees. What else?

1119
01:31:58,879 --> 01:32:00,319
Holly.

1120
01:32:02,119 --> 01:32:06,079
-Holly. What's holly?
-The Christmas stuff.

1121
01:32:06,799 --> 01:32:08,799
Christmas stuff.

1122
01:32:09,599 --> 01:32:11,359
What's that?

1123
01:32:14,599 --> 01:32:17,479
I guess they want us to go to sleep.

1124
01:32:24,039 --> 01:32:29,039
Here you go. We gotta make sure
Captain America's warm in there.

1125
01:32:29,479 --> 01:32:31,239
Can you breathe?

1126
01:32:31,439 --> 01:32:33,679
-You're good?
-Yeah.

1127
01:32:34,119 --> 01:32:36,119
-I gotta go work on the scanner--
-Don't go.

1128
01:32:36,319 --> 01:32:39,519
No, no, no. I'm gonna be
right outside the door.

1129
01:32:39,759 --> 01:32:43,879
All right? I'm just gonna be right there.
I'll leave the door open a little bit.

1130
01:32:44,359 --> 01:32:47,039
And I'll be able to hear you
if you call me.

1131
01:32:47,239 --> 01:32:49,719
I wanna go home.

1132
01:32:51,799 --> 01:32:55,599
But that's why I gotta
work on the scanner.

1133
01:32:56,559 --> 01:32:58,319
All right?

1134
01:32:58,519 --> 01:33:00,479
I'm gonna go out there.

1135
01:33:00,679 --> 01:33:04,039
I'm gonna leave the door open.
I'll be right up the stairs.

1136
01:33:05,119 --> 01:33:06,839
I'll be able to hear you
if you call me.

1137
01:33:07,799 --> 01:33:09,919
-All right?
-All right.

1138
01:33:10,119 --> 01:33:12,479
You gotta trust me, okay?

1139
01:33:12,679 --> 01:33:14,679
You gotta trust me.

1140
01:33:15,559 --> 01:33:18,239
I trust you. I trust you.

1141
01:33:18,439 --> 01:33:19,879
I trust you.

1142
01:33:20,079 --> 01:33:23,079
-I can't hear you.
-I trust you. I trust you.

1143
01:33:26,879 --> 01:33:28,599
Give me a kiss.

1144
01:33:41,279 --> 01:33:44,239
-I'll just be a little while, okay?
-All right.

1145
01:33:44,719 --> 01:33:47,159
-I'll be right here.
-Okay.

1146
01:33:47,359 --> 01:33:49,559
-Can you still hear me?
-Yeah.

1147
01:33:49,759 --> 01:33:51,279
-Can you hear me?
-Yeah.

1148
01:33:51,519 --> 01:33:53,999
-Do you trust me?
-Yeah.

1149
01:34:41,199 --> 01:34:42,839
-Yeah.
-Like that?

1150
01:34:43,079 --> 01:34:46,719
-Yeah, put that....
-Then you go like that.

1151
01:34:46,919 --> 01:34:50,439
-ls that okay?
-I don't know. What do you think?

1152
01:34:50,639 --> 01:34:51,679
Good.

1153
01:34:53,039 --> 01:34:55,279
Let's go. Get your stuff.

1154
01:34:56,519 --> 01:34:59,479
-Hey, why don't you leave it?
-We can't.

1155
01:34:59,679 --> 01:35:01,799
We're gonna have
a different room later.

1156
01:35:01,999 --> 01:35:03,559
Go.

1157
01:35:08,919 --> 01:35:10,279
Hey, Chris.

1158
01:35:10,479 --> 01:35:13,839
-Hey, good morning, Mr. Frakesh.
-What's up?

1159
01:35:14,879 --> 01:35:16,039
Work trip.

1160
01:35:16,239 --> 01:35:18,479
Your wife, Martha, works at
PacBell also, correct?

1161
01:35:18,719 --> 01:35:20,479
-Yes, she does.
-And you guys are both...

1162
01:35:20,679 --> 01:35:22,319
...Iooking to retire at the same time?

1163
01:35:22,519 --> 01:35:24,639
We'd like to retire
and maintain our lifestyle...

1164
01:35:24,839 --> 01:35:26,279
...without paying a lot of taxes.

1165
01:35:26,479 --> 01:35:29,959
So basically, you want nobody's hands
in your pockets but your own?

1166
01:35:30,559 --> 01:35:32,479
Are you familiar with
tax-free municipal...?

1167
01:35:32,679 --> 01:35:34,599
I learned to finish my work quickly.

1168
01:35:34,879 --> 01:35:37,079
I had to finish quickly.

1169
01:35:37,399 --> 01:35:40,919
To get in line at Glide by 5.

1170
01:35:44,639 --> 01:35:46,559
Come on.

1171
01:35:47,039 --> 01:35:48,639
Come on.

1172
01:35:52,719 --> 01:35:55,479
Hold that bus! Hold the bus!

1173
01:35:56,359 --> 01:35:58,119
My Captain America!

1174
01:35:58,359 --> 01:36:00,679
Dad! Dad! Dad!

1175
01:36:00,879 --> 01:36:04,159
Stop it! Shut up! Shut up!

1176
01:36:06,479 --> 01:36:08,519
-Why don't you let the lady in?
-Hey, back up.

1177
01:36:08,719 --> 01:36:11,759
-Hey, man, that's not cool.
-Back up! Back up!

1178
01:36:20,079 --> 01:36:21,559
Come on.

1179
01:36:24,559 --> 01:36:26,799
Dad, we need to get it!

1180
01:36:29,399 --> 01:36:32,039
The important thing about
that freedom train...

1181
01:36:32,239 --> 01:36:34,399
...is it's got to climb mountains.

1182
01:36:34,599 --> 01:36:37,359
We all have to deal with mountains.

1183
01:36:37,559 --> 01:36:40,519
You know, mountains
that go way up high.

1184
01:36:40,919 --> 01:36:42,959
And mountains that go
deep and low.

1185
01:36:43,159 --> 01:36:44,399
-Amen, preacher!
-Yes.

1186
01:36:44,599 --> 01:36:46,919
We know what those mountains are,
here at Glide.

1187
01:36:47,239 --> 01:36:49,359
We sing about them.

1188
01:36:50,119 --> 01:36:55,639
Lord, don't move that mountain

1189
01:36:57,079 --> 01:37:03,479
Give me strength to climb it

1190
01:37:03,999 --> 01:37:10,679
Please don't move
That stumbling block

1191
01:37:10,879 --> 01:37:17,439
But lead me, Lord, around it

1192
01:37:19,079 --> 01:37:24,119
My burdens, they get so heavy

1193
01:37:25,959 --> 01:37:31,599
Seems hard to bear

1194
01:37:32,519 --> 01:37:36,079
But I won't give up
No, no

1195
01:37:36,319 --> 01:37:38,319
Because you promised me

1196
01:37:38,519 --> 01:37:45,279
You'd meet me at the altar of prayer

1197
01:37:45,479 --> 01:37:52,999
-Lord don't move that mountain
-Please don't move that mountain

1198
01:37:53,239 --> 01:37:58,479
But give me strength to climb it

1199
01:38:00,719 --> 01:38:02,719
When's your test?

1200
01:38:03,919 --> 01:38:05,439
T omorrow.

1201
01:38:09,799 --> 01:38:11,599
Are you ready?

1202
01:38:15,519 --> 01:38:16,959
Of course.

1203
01:38:56,039 --> 01:38:57,359
Thank you, sir.

1204
01:39:06,719 --> 01:39:08,919
-Hey. How you doing?
-Hey.

1205
01:39:12,919 --> 01:39:15,919
So did you finish the whole thing,
or you have to go somewhere...?

1206
01:39:16,119 --> 01:39:18,599
I have to go somewhere.

1207
01:39:19,159 --> 01:39:21,999
-But I finished the whole thing too.
-Oh, good.

1208
01:39:22,199 --> 01:39:24,159
-You?
-Yeah.

1209
01:39:24,639 --> 01:39:27,599
-How'd you feel about the graphs?
-Easy.

1210
01:39:28,599 --> 01:39:32,679
I struggled with the essay question
on the back. What did you write?

1211
01:39:32,879 --> 01:39:36,519
-Essay question?
-Yeah, on the back.

1212
01:39:46,439 --> 01:39:47,799
Hey, Chris.

1213
01:39:47,999 --> 01:39:51,279
-Hey. Jeff, right? 49ers game.
-Yeah.

1214
01:39:51,479 --> 01:39:54,959
-Yeah, you were gonna give me a call?
-I never actually got your number.

1215
01:39:56,719 --> 01:39:58,679
Here's my number. Call me, okay?

1216
01:39:58,879 --> 01:40:01,559
Yes, sir. Absolutely.
Thank you very much.

1217
01:40:02,319 --> 01:40:06,079
Chris, you got five bucks?
I left my wallet upstairs.

1218
01:40:06,279 --> 01:40:08,559
Let me run up and grab that
for you, Mr. Frohm.

1219
01:40:08,759 --> 01:40:11,759
No, I gotta be at CAL Bank at 4,
and I'm late.

1220
01:40:17,119 --> 01:40:19,279
-I'll pay you back, honest.
-Five is good?

1221
01:40:19,519 --> 01:40:23,119
Five is lovely. Thank you.
Thank you.

1222
01:40:36,479 --> 01:40:38,959
That's it. That's the room quota.

1223
01:40:39,359 --> 01:40:42,119
There's no more space.
You gotta head out.

1224
01:40:42,319 --> 01:40:45,239
That's it for today.
Come back tomorrow.

1225
01:40:45,439 --> 01:40:48,399
All the rooms are full.
It's completely full.

1226
01:40:48,639 --> 01:40:52,919
That's it. Just keep heading out.
Come back tomorrow.

1227
01:41:27,919 --> 01:41:29,679
You like it?

1228
01:42:20,719 --> 01:42:24,399
Twenty. One, two, three, four.

1229
01:42:27,479 --> 01:42:31,079
Now, here's your bulb,
and there's your ferrite core inductor.

1230
01:42:31,279 --> 01:42:34,079
-How much?
-Eight dollars.

1231
01:42:35,199 --> 01:42:38,519
-What's that?
-It's to repair the light.

1232
01:42:38,719 --> 01:42:40,759
Can I see it?

1233
01:42:42,679 --> 01:42:45,719
Yeah, sure. Just don't break it.

1234
01:42:45,959 --> 01:42:50,439
Unless you wanna sleep in a room
with me for the rest of your life.

1235
01:42:51,639 --> 01:42:53,519
I don't mind.

1236
01:42:53,999 --> 01:42:55,799
Yeah, you will.

1237
01:43:12,119 --> 01:43:14,479
Why don't you
get some sleep, okay?

1238
01:43:14,679 --> 01:43:15,839
Okay.

1239
01:43:16,039 --> 01:43:19,119
-Warm enough?
-Yeah.

1240
01:43:19,399 --> 01:43:21,079
All right.

1241
01:43:23,199 --> 01:43:26,079
Did Mom leave because of me?

1242
01:43:29,439 --> 01:43:33,639
-What?
-Did Mom leave because of me?

1243
01:43:38,199 --> 01:43:42,719
Don't-- Don't even think
something like that.

1244
01:43:43,799 --> 01:43:45,919
Mom left because of Mom.

1245
01:43:46,159 --> 01:43:48,399
And you didn't have anything
to do with that, okay?

1246
01:43:49,119 --> 01:43:50,999
Okay.

1247
01:44:00,839 --> 01:44:02,919
You're a good papa.

1248
01:44:10,759 --> 01:44:12,759
All right, go to sleep.

1249
01:44:13,559 --> 01:44:16,519
-I love you.
-I love you too.

1250
01:45:12,959 --> 01:45:14,959
So far, so good, Chris.

1251
01:45:21,039 --> 01:45:23,599
-lt works.
-Thank you very much.

1252
01:45:23,799 --> 01:45:27,639
Two hundred and fifty dollars.
Four more weeks of oxygen.

1253
01:45:27,959 --> 01:45:32,199
One hundred, 20, 40, 60, 80, 200.

1254
01:45:32,399 --> 01:45:35,159
Twenty, 30, 40, 50.

1255
01:45:36,319 --> 01:45:37,959
-Anything else?
-No, sir.

1256
01:45:38,159 --> 01:45:39,479
Thank you. Thank you.

1257
01:45:39,679 --> 01:45:41,639
-You ready?
-Yep.

1258
01:45:43,559 --> 01:45:46,439
-Are we going to the church place?
-No.

1259
01:45:46,679 --> 01:45:48,639
Where are we going, then?

1260
01:45:49,439 --> 01:45:51,999
-Probably stay at a hotel.
-A hotel?

1261
01:45:52,199 --> 01:45:53,239
Just for the night.

1262
01:45:53,479 --> 01:45:56,239
We can go back to the cave
if you like.

1263
01:45:56,439 --> 01:45:58,159
No, thank you.

1264
01:45:58,359 --> 01:46:00,879
-Ever?
-I hope not.

1265
01:46:01,119 --> 01:46:02,559
Why not?

1266
01:46:02,759 --> 01:46:05,559
Well, because some things are fun
the first time you do them...

1267
01:46:05,759 --> 01:46:08,119
...and then not so much the next.

1268
01:46:08,319 --> 01:46:11,199
-Like the bus?
-Yeah, like the bus.

1269
01:46:11,399 --> 01:46:14,599
I'm sorry, I shouldn't laugh,
should I?

1270
01:46:27,639 --> 01:46:29,319
Sometimes when we're moving
at night...

1271
01:46:29,519 --> 01:46:32,279
...we pass houses with lights
and people.

1272
01:46:33,039 --> 01:46:34,919
Sometimes you can
hear them laugh.

1273
01:46:40,319 --> 01:46:43,679
The next day, after work...

1274
01:46:43,879 --> 01:46:46,119
... we just went to the beach.

1275
01:46:46,319 --> 01:46:48,239
Far away from anything.

1276
01:46:48,439 --> 01:46:49,799
Everything.

1277
01:46:49,999 --> 01:46:51,639
Just Christopher and me.

1278
01:46:53,279 --> 01:46:55,639
-Did you see me?
-Yeah.

1279
01:46:55,879 --> 01:46:58,959
Far away from buses and noise...

1280
01:46:59,159 --> 01:47:04,799
...and a constant disappointment
in my ten-gallon head...

1281
01:47:05,959 --> 01:47:07,839
...and myself.

1282
01:47:08,439 --> 01:47:10,799
-Chris, thank you very much.
-Well, thank you, Dean.

1283
01:47:10,999 --> 01:47:12,839
-Take care.
-You made all the right moves.

1284
01:47:13,039 --> 01:47:14,559
Thanks, Chris.

1285
01:47:16,639 --> 01:47:17,999
Because when I was young...

1286
01:47:18,199 --> 01:47:21,959
...and I'd get an A on a history test
or whatever...

1287
01:47:22,159 --> 01:47:26,759
...I'd get this good feeling about
all the things that I could be.

1288
01:47:28,679 --> 01:47:32,279
And then I never became
any of them.

1289
01:47:39,799 --> 01:47:42,319
-Hey, Chris.
-Hey.

1290
01:47:42,559 --> 01:47:45,159
-How you doing, Jay?
-I'm doing fine.

1291
01:47:45,359 --> 01:47:49,519
Rumor has it you signed 31 accounts
for us from Pacific Bell.

1292
01:47:49,719 --> 01:47:51,159
Yeah, yeah.

1293
01:47:51,359 --> 01:47:55,159
Met some guys at a ball game,
got some cards. I've been working.

1294
01:47:55,359 --> 01:47:56,999
I guess.

1295
01:47:59,959 --> 01:48:02,199
So one more day.

1296
01:48:02,399 --> 01:48:03,999
Getting nervous?

1297
01:48:04,559 --> 01:48:06,919
-No, I'm okay.
-Yeah?

1298
01:48:07,119 --> 01:48:09,079
Listen, whatever happens...

1299
01:48:09,279 --> 01:48:11,719
...you've done a fantastic job, Chris.

1300
01:48:11,919 --> 01:48:13,479
I mean that.

1301
01:48:14,319 --> 01:48:16,119
Take care of yourself.

1302
01:48:31,119 --> 01:48:34,319
Yes, Mr. Johnson.
Chris Gardner, Dean Witter.

1303
01:48:34,639 --> 01:48:36,719
Yes, sir. Just calling
to thank you very much...

1304
01:48:36,919 --> 01:48:39,439
...for your support
at last month's seminar.

1305
01:48:39,959 --> 01:48:41,639
Yes, sir. Absolutely.

1306
01:48:42,279 --> 01:48:43,879
Yes, sir.

1307
01:48:44,119 --> 01:48:45,479
No, sir, that's it.

1308
01:48:45,679 --> 01:48:48,159
Thank you very much. Bye-bye.

1309
01:48:49,759 --> 01:48:52,639
Chris. Come.

1310
01:49:20,039 --> 01:49:23,119
-Hi, Chris.
-Mr. Frohm, good to see you.

1311
01:49:24,279 --> 01:49:26,199
-Nice shirt.
-Thank you, sir.

1312
01:49:26,399 --> 01:49:27,599
-Chris.
-Hey, Jay.

1313
01:49:28,039 --> 01:49:32,319
-Chris.
-Chris, sit down, please.

1314
01:49:35,239 --> 01:49:39,319
I thought I'd wear a shirt today.

1315
01:49:39,519 --> 01:49:41,479
You know,
being the last day and all.

1316
01:49:41,679 --> 01:49:45,039
Well, thank you. Thank you.
We appreciate that.

1317
01:49:45,919 --> 01:49:47,679
But...

1318
01:49:47,919 --> 01:49:50,679
...wear one tomorrow though, okay?

1319
01:49:50,919 --> 01:49:53,839
Because tomorrow's
going to be your first day...

1320
01:49:54,559 --> 01:49:57,799
...if you'd like to work here
as a broker.

1321
01:49:59,159 --> 01:50:00,959
Would you like that, Chris?

1322
01:50:01,879 --> 01:50:03,479
Yes, sir.

1323
01:50:03,679 --> 01:50:07,039
Good. We couldn't be happier.

1324
01:50:08,039 --> 01:50:11,199
So welcome.

1325
01:50:13,079 --> 01:50:18,039
-Was it as easy as it looked?
-No, sir. No, sir, it wasn't.

1326
01:50:20,399 --> 01:50:22,799
-Good luck, Chris.
-Thank you. Thank you.

1327
01:50:29,199 --> 01:50:31,079
Oh, Chris.

1328
01:50:33,599 --> 01:50:35,679
I almost forgot.

1329
01:50:37,719 --> 01:50:39,279
Thank you.

1330
01:50:59,679 --> 01:51:01,879
This part of my life...

1331
01:51:02,759 --> 01:51:04,959
...this little part...

1332
01:51:08,319 --> 01:51:10,959
...is called "Happiness. "

1333
01:51:57,679 --> 01:52:01,279
Christopher. Christopher.
Come here.

1334
01:52:30,959 --> 01:52:33,359
So how many...

1335
01:52:33,559 --> 01:52:35,519
...planets are there?

1336
01:52:36,799 --> 01:52:38,599
-Seven.
-Seven?

1337
01:52:39,119 --> 01:52:40,919
Nine.

1338
01:52:43,319 --> 01:52:45,359
Who's the king of the jungle?

1339
01:52:45,759 --> 01:52:48,519
-Gorilla.
-The gorilla?

1340
01:52:48,799 --> 01:52:50,199
The gorilla?

1341
01:52:50,399 --> 01:52:52,079
No. Lion.

1342
01:52:52,279 --> 01:52:54,879
Oh, yeah. Lion, lion, lion.

1343
01:52:56,959 --> 01:52:59,959
Hey, Dad, listen to this.
Knock, knock.

1344
01:53:00,159 --> 01:53:02,079
-Who's there?
-Shelby.

1345
01:53:02,279 --> 01:53:03,399
Shelby who?

1346
01:53:03,599 --> 01:53:07,399
Shelby coming around the mountain
When she comes

1347
01:53:08,239 --> 01:53:09,599
-Knock knock.
-Who's there?

1348
01:53:09,799 --> 01:53:12,279
-Nobody.
-Nobody who?

1349
01:53:13,159 --> 01:53:14,919
Nobody who?

1350
01:53:18,239 --> 01:53:21,199
Now, that's funny. I like that one.
